      "math_academy_id": "q-96862",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.7630$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.7630$ lies between. These numbers are $0.7611$ and $0.7642.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.7611 & <0.7630<0.7642\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.71) & <Φ(z)<Φ(0.72).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{0.71+0.72}{2}=0.715.\n$$",
